&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Managing Editor, Character IP to lead Duolingo&#39;s manga and anime expansion in Japan. This isn&#39;t a role for someone who manages timelines and coordinates vendors from a distance. You&#39;ll get into the weeds — developing Duo&#39;s Japanese character voice, writing plots when needed, identifying the right manga artists, and building the studio and TV network relationships that turn a great concept into something millions of people actually watch. Our roadmap goes manga first, then anime, with a TV morning show slot (think Chiikawa) as the target format for animation. This role reports into the Director of Design Studio Brand team, with a dotted line to the Director of Country Marketing Japan and Korea team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧠&amp;nbsp; You will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and uphold Duolingo’s high quality bar across all creative projects in this pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Design Studio Creative Directors to define Duo&#39;s Japanese character profile — tone of voice, personality details, backstory — while staying true to his globally established character bible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write your own plots and lead original story development when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scout and brief manga artists and illustrators who match the look and feel we&#39;re going for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage relationships with publishers and editors to get manga projects off the ground&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select and manage anime production studios — handling contracts, budgets, schedules, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch to and build relationships with TV networks, with the goal of securing a morning show slot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set visual quality standards appropriate to each format and platform (TV, streaming, short-form)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep global and local stakeholders aligned and get buy-in at the right moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✅&amp;nbsp; You have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on manga editing / directing experience at a publisher, editorial production company, or IP firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop original stories — you&#39;ve written plots yourself, not just managed others who do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharp editorial / directorial instincts for capturing a character&#39;s voice and making it feel alive on the page&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real relationships with publishers, manga artists, and writers, and a track record of getting projects made&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of anime production: studio contracts, budgets, and how to get quality work at a fair value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing connections with major TV networks and experience pitching concepts for broadcast slots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional collaboration skills, seeking consensus and feedback when making decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level English&amp;nbsp; needed for collaborating with our global team — strong written English vs. spoken fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐&amp;nbsp; Exceptional candidates will have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a manga property all the way through to anime adaptation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with social-native formats (vertical, short-form, platform-specific)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in brand licensing, merchandise, or IP business development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with inbound or outbound IP localization (foreign IP in Japan or Japanese IP abroad)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
