&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Duolingo’s business runs on two numbers: Daily Active Users and revenue. This role owns both. As VP of Product for Growth and Monetization, you&#39;ll lead our largest product organization through a team of experienced pillar leads. Your teams shape how learners come back every day and why they choose to pay. You&#39;ll run one of the highest-velocity experimentation engines in consumer tech, with a mandate to grow DAUs and revenue sustainably and never at the expense of learners. This role reports to the Chief Product Officer, joins Duolingo&#39;s Product Leadership and Senior Leadership Team (SLT), and is based in New York, NY or Pittsburgh, PA on a hybrid (4+1) schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧠&amp;nbsp; You will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own DAUs and revenue, Duolingo&#39;s two hero metrics, and deliver both against forecast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the pillar leads who run Growth and Monetization, an org of roughly 20 PMs and our largest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop senior product leaders, and raise the bar for product talent across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Design leadership to make clear tradeoffs and ship quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build world-class product operating mechanisms: Clear north star metrics, planning and review rituals, and rigorous A/B testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allocate resources across Growth and Monetization, balancing steady optimization with bigger swings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the single voice for Growth and Monetization at the executive level: progress, risks, and the plan to hit both numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✅&amp;nbsp; You have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive product leadership in consumer tech, with multi-year measurable impact on DAUs or revenue at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High judgment and operational rigor, with a record of hitting forecasts without sacrificing user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading managers of managers and developing strong product leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading through change: reorgs, new operating models, faster execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional range, aligning Product, Engineering, Design, Data, and Marketing on clear priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in growth and monetization for freemium and subscription products, grounded in experimentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work from or relocate to New York, NY or Pittsburgh, PA on a hybrid (4+1) schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
